# Secrets. This gate stands regardless of the public-data decision: a live D1Baseball
# session cookie or a Supabase service key in a public repo is a different problem from
# public athlete data. Verified with `git ls-files` + gitleaks before the first push.
config.yaml
config.local.yaml
.env
.env.*
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*-service-account.json
profiles.yml
# warehouse/profiles.example.yml ships instead and is copied into place by the quickstart,
# so `dbt build` still runs from a fresh clone without a real profile ever being tracked.

# Databases. 128MB of SQLite plus dbt's local duckdb; both rebuild from the pipeline.
db/*.db
db/*.bak*
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# Regenerable build and cache output
dist/
.netlify/
warehouse/target/
warehouse/logs/
warehouse/dbt_packages/
data/cache/
data/ncaa_cache/

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Notebook checkpoints. Committed notebooks are outputs-stripped on the way in
# (scripts/build_consolidated_repo.py), so a diff shows code, not base64 images.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# NOT ignored, deliberately, reversing the old repo's blanket data ban:
#   data/**            real TrackMan and portal exports, so the apps run from a clone
#   *.csv *.xlsx       usd_baseball_TM_master_file.csv, USDHITTINGYTD.csv and friends
#   *.txt              the stat-page pastes the parsers are tested against
#   apps/*/models/**   the 10 trained model artifacts
# Trevor cleared public real data and USD branding on 2026-09-12. A repo whose apps
# cannot start from a fresh clone is a demo nobody can run.
